## Maximum Number of Badges [/{apiKey}/{idType}/{posterType}/{mediaId}.jpg{?badges,maxBadges}]

**Only supported with Tier 3+**

The maximum number of badges to show at once on an image, the default value for this differs based on rating bar position and image type.

The value is expected to be a number, example: `1`, `2`, `3`, `4`, etc

+ Parameters
    + apiKey (required, string) ... The user's API Key
    + idType (required, string, `imdb`) ... The requesting id type, can be: `imdb`, `tmdb`, `tvdb`
    + posterType (required, string, `poster-default`) ... The poster rating type, can be: `poster-default`, `poster-certs`, `poster-mc`, `poster-rt`, `textless-default`, `textless-certs`, `textless-mc`, `textless-rt`
    + mediaId (required, string, `tt2395427`) ... The ID for the movie / series, depending on the chosen `idType`, when using the `tmdb` or `tvdb` id types you should also include the media type in the ID (TMDB/TVDB ID examples: `movie-155` or `series-155`)
    + badges (required, string, `4k`) ... Badge tags separated by , (comma)
    + maxBadges (required, string, `2`) ... Maximum badges, can be: `1`, `2`, `3`, `4`, etc

### Example [GET]

+ Response 200 (image/jpeg)


## Badge Position [/{apiKey}/{idType}/{posterType}/{mediaId}.jpg{?badges,badgePos}]

**Only supported with Tier 3+**

The badge position can be set with the `?badgePos=` query parameter and works for both posters and backdrops.

Supported badge positions: `left` (default), `center`, `right`, `bottom|left`, `bottom|center`, `bottom|right`

[Example for Left Badges](https://ratingposterdb.com/static/tier-3-badge-left.jpg)

[Example for Center Badges](https://ratingposterdb.com/static/tier-3-badge-center.jpg)

[Example for Right Badges](https://ratingposterdb.com/static/tier-3-badge-right.jpg)

+ Parameters
    + apiKey (required, string) ... The user's API Key
    + idType (required, string, `imdb`) ... The requesting id type, can be: `imdb`, `tmdb`, `tvdb`
    + posterType (required, string, `poster-default`) ... The poster rating type, can be: `poster-default`, `poster-certs`, `poster-mc`, `poster-rt`, `textless-default`, `textless-certs`, `textless-mc`, `textless-rt`
    + mediaId (required, string, `tt2395427`) ... The ID for the movie / series, depending on the chosen `idType`, when using the `tmdb` or `tvdb` id types you should also include the media type in the ID (TMDB/TVDB ID examples: `movie-155` or `series-155`)
    + badges (required, string, `4k`) ... Badge tags separated by , (comma)
    + badgePos (required, string, `center`) ... Badge position, can be: `left` (default), `center`, `right`

### Example [GET]

+ Response 200 (image/jpeg)


## TMDB Poster Choices [/{apiKey}/{idType}/{posterType}/tmdb-poster/{mediaId}/{tmdbPosterFilename}]

**Only supported with Tier 2+**

+ Parameters
    + apiKey (required, string) ... The user's API Key
    + idType (required, string, `imdb`) ... The requesting id type, can be: `imdb`, `tmdb`, `tvdb`
    + posterType (required, string, `poster-default`) ... The poster rating type, can be: `poster-default`, `poster-certs`, `poster-mc`, `poster-rt`, `textless-default`, `textless-certs`, `textless-mc`, `textless-rt`
    + mediaId (required, string, `tt2395427`) ... The ID for the movie / series, depending on the chosen `idType`, when using the `tmdb` or `tvdb` id types you should also include the media type in the ID (TMDB/TVDB ID examples: `movie-155` or `series-155`)
    + tmdbPosterFilename (required, string, `kqjL17yufvn9OVLyXYpvtyrFfak.jpg`) ... The image filename from the [TMDB Poster Image Response](https://developers.themoviedb.org/3/getting-started/images)

### Example [GET]

+ Response 200 (image/jpeg)


## Custom Poster Images [/{apiKey}/{idType}/{posterType}/custom-poster/{mediaId}.jpg{?img}]

**Only supported with Tier 3+**

The `?img=` query parameter needs to be set to an image URI (URL encoded).

+ Parameters
    + apiKey (required, string) ... The user's API Key
    + idType (required, string, `imdb`) ... The requesting id type, can be: `imdb`, `tmdb`, `tvdb`
    + posterType (required, string, `poster-default`) ... The poster rating type, can be: `poster-default`, `poster-certs`, `poster-mc`, `poster-rt`, `textless-default`, `textless-certs`, `textless-mc`, `textless-rt`
    + mediaId (required, string, `tt2395427`) ... The ID for the movie / series, depending on the chosen `idType`, when using the `tmdb` or `tvdb` id types you should also include the media type in the ID (TMDB/TVDB ID examples: `movie-155` or `series-155`)
    + img (required, string, `https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/RYMX2wcKCBAr24UyPD7xwmjaTn.jpg`) ... Any image URI to use as poster

### Example [GET]

+ Response 200 (image/jpeg)


## Backdrops with Ratings [/{apiKey}/{idType}/{backdropType}/{mediaId}.jpg]

**Only supported with Tier 2+**

[Example of Backdrop](https://ratingposterdb.com/static/tier-2-backdrop.jpg)

Note: as with posters, backdrops also support custom ratings choice, rating order, as well as all Tier 3 customisation such as choosing where the ratings are shown and the color of the rating background and text color.

+ Parameters
    + apiKey (required, string) ... The user's API Key
    + idType (required, string, `imdb`) ... The requesting id type, can be: `imdb`, `tmdb`, `tvdb`
    + backdropType (required, string, `backdrop-default`) ... The backdrop type, currently only `backdrop-default` is supported
    + mediaId (required, string, `tt2395427`) ... The ID for the movie / series, depending on the chosen `idType`, when using the `tmdb` or `tvdb` id types you should also include the media type in the ID (TMDB/TVDB ID examples: `movie-155` or `series-155`)

### Example [GET]

+ Response 200 (image/jpeg)


## Logos with Ratings [/{apiKey}/{idType}/{logoType}/{mediaId}.png]

**Only supported with Tier 2+**

Note: compared to posters and backdrops which are JPG, it is important to note that logos are PNG images as they require transparency.

Note 2: due to limited space in the logo image, logos do not support badges

Note 3: as with posters, logos also support custom ratings choice, rating order, as well as all Tier 3 customisation such as choosing where the ratings are shown and the color of the rating background and text color.

[Example of Logo](https://ratingposterdb.com/static/tier-2-logo.png)

+ Parameters
    + apiKey (required, string) ... The user's API Key
    + idType (required, string, `imdb`) ... The requesting id type, can be: `imdb`, `tmdb`, `tvdb`
    + logoType (required, string, `logo-default`) ... The logo type, currently only `logo-default` is supported
    + mediaId (required, string, `tt2395427`) ... The ID for the movie / series, depending on the chosen `idType`, when using the `tmdb` or `tvdb` id types you should also include the media type in the ID (TMDB/TVDB ID examples: `movie-155` or `series-155`)

### Example [GET]

+ Response 200 (image/png)


## Anime Ratings [/{apikey}/{idType}/{posterType}/{mediaId}.jpg]

All known anime movies and series include MAL rating by default (except for the free tier), so the API is the same as in the "Posters with Ratings" category of this page.

In the case of anime, instead of receiving IMDB + RT + MC ratings, you will receive MAL + IMDB + RT (+ MC if any other rating is missing) with the following poster types: `poster-default`, `poster-certs`, `poster-rt`, `poster-mc`, `backdrop-default`, `textless-default`, `textless-certs`, `textless-rt`, `textless-mc`.

This applies for all Tiers.

+ Parameters
    + apikey (required, string) ... The user's API Key
    + idType (required, string, `imdb`) ... The requesting id type, can be: `imdb`, `tmdb`, `tvdb`
    + posterType (required, string, `poster-default`) ... The poster rating type, can be: `poster-default`, `poster-certs`, `poster-mc`, `poster-rt`, `textless-default`, `textless-certs`, `textless-mc`, `textless-rt`
    + mediaId (required, string, `tt2395427`) ... The ID for the movie / series, depending on the chosen `idType`, when using the `tmdb` or `tvdb` id types you should also include the media type in the ID (TMDB/TVDB ID examples: `movie-155` or `series-155`)

### Example [GET]

+ Response 200 (image/jpeg)


## More Ratings [/{apiKey}/{idType}/{imageType}/{mediaId}.jpg{?order}]

**Only supported with Tier 1+**

The `?order=` query parameter needs to be set to a text that includes one or more rating tags, split by comma. This querystring parameter works with `rating-order` image type for posters, `backdrop-default` image type for backdrops and `logo-default` image type for logos.

Example order query parameter values:
- `myanimelist,imdb,commonsense,letterboxd`
- `imdb,tmdb,trakt`

Currently available rating tags:
- `imdb` : IMDB audience rating
- `tmdb` : TMDB audience rating
- `trakt` : Trakt audience rating
- `tomatoes-critics` : Rotten Tomaotes critics rating
- `tomatoes-audience` : Rotten Tomaotes audience rating
- `metacritic-critics` : Metacritic critics rating
- `metacritic-audience` : Metacritic audience rating
- `letterboxd` : Letterboxd audience rating
- `rogerebert` : Roger Ebert rating
- `myanimelist` : MyAnimeList audience rating
- `commonsense` : Common Sense Media age rating
- `mdblist` : MDBList rating
- `us-age` : US age rating
- `overall-rating` : overall rating (based on all audience and critics scores)
- `critics-rating` : overall critics rating (based on all critics scores)
- `audience-rating` : overall audience rating (based on all audience scores)

+ Parameters
    + apiKey (required, string) ... The user's API Key
    + idType (required, string, `imdb`) ... The requesting id type, can be: `imdb`, `tmdb`, `tvdb`
    + imageType (required, string, `rating-order`) ... For posters use `rating-order`, for backdrops use `backdrop-default`
    + mediaId (required, string, `tt2395427`) ... The ID for the movie / series, depending on the chosen `idType`, when using the `tmdb` or `tvdb` id types you should also include the media type in the ID (TMDB/TVDB ID examples: `movie-155` or `series-155`)
    + order (required, string, `myanimelist,imdb,commonsense,letterboxd`) ... Text including one or more rating tags

### Example [GET]

+ Response 200 (image/jpeg)


## Image Size [/{apiKey}/{idType}/poster-certs/{mediaId}.jpg{?imageSize}]

**Only supported with Tier 2+**

Poster image sizes:
- `medium`: 580x859 (default)
- `large`: 1280x1896 (Tier 2+)
- `verylarge`: 2000x2962 (Tier 3+)

Backdrop image sizes:
- `medium`: 1920x1080 (default)
- `small`: 1280x720 (Tier 2+)
- `large`: 3840x2160 (Tier 3+)

Logo image sizes:
- `medium`: 780x244 (default)
- `large`: 1722x539 (Tier 2+)
- `verylarge`: 2689x841 (Tier 3+)

+ Parameters
    + apiKey (required, string) ... The user's API Key
    + idType (required, string, `imdb`) ... The requesting id type, can be: `imdb`, `tmdb`, `tvdb`
    + mediaId (required, string, `tt2395427`) ... The ID for the movie / series, depending on the chosen `idType`, when using the `tmdb` or `tvdb` id types you should also include the media type in the ID (TMDB/TVDB ID examples: `movie-155` or `series-155`)
    + imageSize (required, string, `large`) ... Text including preferred image size

### Example [GET]

+ Response 200 (image/jpeg)


