## Font Style [/{apiKey}/{idType}/poster-certs/{mediaId}.jpg{?textStyle}]

**Only supported with Tier 2+**

Supported values:
- `0` : Default, will show ratings in the form of: 7.4/10, 75%, 2/5, etc
- `1` : Normalizes ratings to all be between 1-100 and removes "/5", "/10", "%" suffix, examples: 75, 12, 39
- `2` : Only remove "/5" and "/10" suffix, examples: 7.4, 75%, 2.2, etc

+ Parameters
    + apiKey (required, string) ... The user's API Key
    + idType (required, string, `imdb`) ... The requesting id type, can be: `imdb`, `tmdb`, `tvdb`
    + mediaId (required, string, `tt2395427`) ... The ID for the movie / series, depending on the chosen `idType`, when using the `tmdb` or `tvdb` id types you should also include the media type in the ID (TMDB/TVDB ID examples: `movie-155` or `series-155`)
    + textStyle (required, string, `1`) ... Font Style, can be: `0`, `1`, `2`

### Example [GET]

+ Response 200 (image/jpeg)


## Rating Bar Position [/{apiKey}/{idType}/poster-certs/{mediaId}.jpg{?ratingBarPos}]

**Only supported with Tier 3+**

Poster image rating bar positions:
- `bottom` (default)
- `top`
- `left-top`
- `left-center`
- `left-bottom`
- `right-top`
- `right-center`
- `right-bottom`

Backdrop image rating bar positions:
- `right-top` (default)
- `right-center`
- `right-bottom`
- `left-top`
- `left-center`
- `left-bottom`

Logo image rating bar positions:
- `bottom` (default)
- `top`
- `left-top`
- `left-center`
- `left-bottom`
- `right-top`
- `right-center`
- `right-bottom`
- `bottom-left`
- `bottom-right`
- `top-left`
- `top-right`

+ Parameters
    + apiKey (required, string) ... The user's API Key
    + idType (required, string, `imdb`) ... The requesting id type, can be: `imdb`, `tmdb`, `tvdb`
    + mediaId (required, string, `tt2395427`) ... The ID for the movie / series, depending on the chosen `idType`, when using the `tmdb` or `tvdb` id types you should also include the media type in the ID (TMDB/TVDB ID examples: `movie-155` or `series-155`)
    + ratingBarPos (required, string, `top`) ... Text including preferred rating bar position

### Example [GET]

+ Response 200 (image/jpeg)


## Rating Bar Opacity [/{apiKey}/{idType}/poster-certs/{mediaId}.jpg{?ratingBarOpacity}]

**Only supported with Tier 3+**

Rating bar opacity is set with a float value (ex: `0.5`, `0.2`).

While `0.0` or `0` are not supported, using `0.01` will make the rating bar completely transparent.

While `1.0` or `1` are not supported, using `0.99` will make the rating bar remove transparency.

Both posters and backdrops support `?ratingBarOpacity=`

+ Parameters
    + apiKey (required, string) ... The user's API Key
    + idType (required, string, `imdb`) ... The requesting id type, can be: `imdb`, `tmdb`, `tvdb`
    + mediaId (required, string, `tt2395427`) ... The ID for the movie / series, depending on the chosen `idType`, when using the `tmdb` or `tvdb` id types you should also include the media type in the ID (TMDB/TVDB ID examples: `movie-155` or `series-155`)
    + ratingBarOpacity (required, string, `0.5`) ... Text including preferred rating bar opacity

### Example [GET]

+ Response 200 (image/jpeg)


## Rating Bar Background Color [/{apiKey}/{idType}/poster-certs/{mediaId}.jpg{?ratingBarColor}]

**Only supported with Tier 3+**

The rating bar background color is set with a text value for the HTML color name (ex: `red`, `blue`) or the hex value of the color (ex: `#FFE4C4`).

Both posters and backdrops support `?ratingBarColor=`

+ Parameters
    + apiKey (required, string) ... The user's API Key
    + idType (required, string, `imdb`) ... The requesting id type, can be: `imdb`, `tmdb`, `tvdb`
    + mediaId (required, string, `tt2395427`) ... The ID for the movie / series, depending on the chosen `idType`, when using the `tmdb` or `tvdb` id types you should also include the media type in the ID (TMDB/TVDB ID examples: `movie-155` or `series-155`)
    + ratingBarColor (required, string, `blue`) ... Text including preferred rating bar color

### Example [GET]

+ Response 200 (image/jpeg)


## Rating Bar Type [/{apiKey}/{idType}/poster-certs/{mediaId}.jpg{?ratingBarType}]

**Only supported with Tier 3+**

The rating bar type can be either "bar" (default) or "blocks". The "blocks" type supports exclusive settings such as "ratingBarRoundness" and "ratingBarPadding".

+ Parameters
    + apiKey (required, string) ... The user's API Key
    + idType (required, string, `imdb`) ... The requesting id type, can be: `imdb`, `tmdb`, `tvdb`
    + mediaId (required, string, `tt2395427`) ... The ID for the movie / series, depending on the chosen `idType`, when using the `tmdb` or `tvdb` id types you should also include the media type in the ID (TMDB/TVDB ID examples: `movie-155` or `series-155`)
    + ratingBarType (required, string, `blocks`) ... Rating bar type (either `bar` or `blocks`)

### Example [GET]

+ Response 200 (image/jpeg)


## Rating Bar Roundness [/{apiKey}/{idType}/poster-certs/{mediaId}.jpg{?ratingBarRoundness}]

**Only supported with Tier 3+**

The rating bar roundness applies only for "blocks" ratingBarType or supported themes (that include "blocks" or "stripes" in the name), it can be set to "default" (minimal rounded corners), "full" (completely rounded corners) or any number (pixels) including "0" (sharp corners).

+ Parameters
    + apiKey (required, string) ... The user's API Key
    + idType (required, string, `imdb`) ... The requesting id type, can be: `imdb`, `tmdb`, `tvdb`
    + mediaId (required, string, `tt2395427`) ... The ID for the movie / series, depending on the chosen `idType`, when using the `tmdb` or `tvdb` id types you should also include the media type in the ID (TMDB/TVDB ID examples: `movie-155` or `series-155`)
    + ratingBarRoundness (required, string, `full`) ... Rating block corner roundness for supported themes

### Example [GET]

+ Response 200 (image/jpeg)


## Rating Bar Padding [/{apiKey}/{idType}/poster-certs/{mediaId}.jpg{?ratingBarPadding}]

**Only supported with Tier 3+**

The rating block padding applies only for "blocks" ratingBarType or supported themes (that include "blocks" or "stripes" in the name), it can be set to any number (pixels) including "0".

