## Logo Styles [/{apiKey}/{idType}/poster-certs/{mediaId}.jpg{?logoStyle}]

**Only supported with Tier 3+**

Setting this value to "1" will make the rating logos round, setting this value to "2" will disable the logos.

+ Parameters
    + apiKey (required, string) ... The user's API Key
    + idType (required, string, `imdb`) ... The requesting id type, can be: `imdb`, `tmdb`, `tvdb`
    + mediaId (required, string, `tt2395427`) ... The ID for the movie / series, depending on the chosen `idType`, when using the `tmdb` or `tvdb` id types you should also include the media type in the ID (TMDB/TVDB ID examples: `movie-155` or `series-155`)
    + logoStyle (required, string, `1`) ... If rating logo should be a round image or disabled

### Example [GET]

+ Response 200 (image/jpeg)


## Backdrop Certificates Position [/{apiKey}/{idType}/backdrop-default/{mediaId}.jpg{?certsPos}]

**Only supported with Tier 3+**

The certificates (such as "certified fresh" or "must watch") from the backdrops can be moved with the `certsPos` query parameter.

Only backdrops support `?certsPos=`.

Available positions for backdrop certificates:
- `left` (default)
- `right`

+ Parameters
    + apiKey (required, string) ... The user's API Key
    + idType (required, string, `imdb`) ... The requesting id type, can be: `imdb`, `tmdb`, `tvdb`
    + mediaId (required, string, `tt2395427`) ... The ID for the movie / series, depending on the chosen `idType`, when using the `tmdb` or `tvdb` id types you should also include the media type in the ID (TMDB/TVDB ID examples: `movie-155` or `series-155`)
    + certsPos (required, string, `right`) ... Text including preferred backdrop certificate position

### Example [GET]

+ Response 200 (image/jpeg)
